{
  "id": "battle-festa",
  "name": "Battle Festa",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Festa was the Pokémon Card Game's year-end festival in Japan in the XY era, held in 2013, 2014 and 2015 after the last Battle Carnival: free, day-long events at exhibition halls in two to five cities, where every visitor got an original card. Its main tournament, the Victory Battle, ran in two leagues through stages of winning streaks to a single-elimination Climax Stage, with an Item card as the prize for a win, and the top three of each league on each day won Victory Ring in gold, silver or bronze, stamped with the event's name. Side battles earned Play Points that bought more cards. In 2014 the tournament was tied to the Pokémon Card Gym shops, and in 2015 a second tournament, the CoroCoro Challenge, gave Victory Rings of its own.",
    "sources": [
